Z||000010||2birds||02-11-2000||11:21 PM||||I paid $150 a month when I was 20, back in 1988 and first bought my Plastic Poncho, and I had a clean record.  It dropped to under $100 when I turned 21, and around $60 when I got married.  I pay $240 every six months, $250 deductible, last accident just over 6 years ago, last ticket just over 7 years ago.  I've been with State Farm for 12 years now, and I'm 32 and married.  I also have every other type of insurance with the same agent, so every little discount helps.  My 97 T-bird costs about $20 a month more than the Fiero.  I keep full coverage because it's dirt cheap, and the minute I drop it, some pulp wood hauler will drop a log on me. ||||reg||1
